  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ResCoordDisc 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You currently serve as a research coordinator for a university lab that
    is exploring several early drug ideas for lung cancer. You keep careful records
    about which ideas are showing the most promise and help prepare reports that
    may later support preclinical studies. Even though you don\u2019t play a direct
    role in the early research, research coordinators help document and share early
    discoveries in ways that allow the research to safely move toward testing in
    animals \u2014 and eventually humans.\n\nIs this true or false?"
  explanation: During the discovery stage, research coordinators help organize data,
    keep records up to date, and make sure lab teams communicate well with each other.
    Their work helps the science stay reliable and well-structured as it moves toward
    future preclinical testing. By supporting clear communication and organization,
    they help early research run smoothly and stay on track.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
